   --- SOVEREIGN RECIPROCAL COMMONS RIDER (SRCL-1.0) ---

   Section 10. Express Conditions Precedent (Jacobsen v. Katzer Doctrine)
   All permissions, grants, and licenses conferred by this document are subject
   to the express conditions precedent set forth in Sections 11, 12, 13, and 14.
   Any use, reproduction, preparation of Derivative Works, distribution, or
   AI model training outside of or in breach of these conditions is unpermitted,
   void ab initio, and constitutes willful copyright infringement under 17 U.S.C.
   § 106 and § 501.

   Section 11. Reciprocal Source Transparency ("Open Improvements")
   Commercial use, monetization, deployment, and operation of this Work are
   expressly authorized and encouraged for all individuals and enterprises.
   You are fully permitted to monetize software, offer hosted services, and build
   profitable commercial applications incorporating this Work. However, if You
   modify, enhance, or optimize the Source code of this Work and deploy, execute,
   or distribute such modifications as part of any commercial software, networked
   SaaS application, or hosted API service, You must make the Source code of
   Your modifications to this Work publicly available under these same license
   terms within thirty (30) days of public or commercial deployment.

   Section 12. Reciprocal AI Weight Release ($25M Mega-Corporation Clause)
   (a) Scope and Definitions: For the purposes of this Section:
       (i) "AI Training" means using the Source code, Object code, architectural
           specifications, synthetic reasoning traces, test suites, or outputs
           of this Work to train, pre-train, fine-tune, distill, align, optimize,
           or reinforce any neural network, machine learning model, or generative
           foundation model.
       (ii) "Model Weights" means all learned numerical parameters, tensors,
           biases, checkpoint files, embedding layers, and tokenizer definitions
           governing inference.
       (iii) "Qualifying Enterprise" means any commercial enterprise, corporation,
           joint venture, foundation AI research laboratory, or affiliated Legal
           Entity with annual gross revenues, aggregate raised investment capital,
           or balance-sheet valuation exceeding twenty-five million United States
           Dollars ($25,000,000 USD).

   (b) Condition of Weight Release: If a Qualifying Enterprise conducts AI
       Training upon this Work or its Derivative Works, it is an express condition
       of this License that such Qualifying Enterprise must publish and release the
       resulting Model Weights, architecture specifications, and inference recipes
       openly to the general public under an OSI-approved open source license or
       permissive OpenRAIL / Apache-compatible license within thirty (30) days
       of commercial availability, internal production use, or public release.

   (c) Safe Harbor for Builders and Startups: Individual developers, open-source
       collaborators, academic institutions, non-profit organizations, and
       commercial enterprises with annual gross revenues and capital below
       twenty-five million United States Dollars ($25,000,000 USD) are explicitly
       exempt from this Model Weight release condition.

   (d) Automatic License Forfeiture: Failure of a Qualifying Enterprise to satisfy
       the condition in subsection (b) results in immediate, automatic, and
       retroactive termination of all copyright, patent, and trademark licenses
       granted herein. Any continued reproduction, distribution, inference hosting,
       or commercial utilization of models derived from such training constitutes
       willful copyright infringement under Title 17 of the United States Code.

   Section 13. Retroactive Inception and Legal Integration
   This License applies retroactively to all prior commits, branches, releases,
   tags, and historical distributions of this Work from the moment of initial
   creation and repository genesis. Licensor hereby waives, supersedes, and
   extinguishes all prior restrictive or noncommercial license notices across
   all historical versions in favor of this Sovereign Reciprocal Commons License.
   All compliant developers, users, and contributors are granted full retroactive
   covenant and release for past distributions under these terms.

   Section 14. Statutory Damages and Sovereign Enforcement
   Any Qualifying Enterprise that conducts unauthorized AI Training on this Work
   in violation of Section 12 agrees that such infringement is willful, knowing,
   and subject to maximum statutory damages of up to one hundred fifty thousand
   United States Dollars ($150,000 USD) per infringed work pursuant to 17 U.S.C.
   § 504(c)(2), in addition to full accounting and disgorgement of all profits
   attributable to the infringement and permanent injunctive relief under 17
   U.S.C. § 502.

   Section 15. Prevailing Party Legal Fees and Costs
   In any legal proceeding, arbitration, or judicial action brought to enforce
   the terms of this License or for copyright infringement arising from breach
   of the conditions precedent herein, the prevailing party shall be entitled to
   an award of its reasonable attorney fees, expert witness fees, and litigation
   costs pursuant to 17 U.S.C. § 505 and applicable law.

   Section 16. Severability and Preservation of Grant
   If any provision, sentence, or clause of this Rider is held invalid, illegal,
   or unenforceable by a court of competent jurisdiction, such invalidity shall
   not affect any other provision of this License. The remaining provisions
   shall remain in full legal force and effect, and the invalid clause shall be
   reformed to the minimum extent necessary to achieve its economic intent.

   Section 17. Governing Law and Exclusive Venue
   This License, and all claims or causes of action arising out of or related to
